7592186045417] [17592186424254 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424254 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424254 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424254 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186424249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424254 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e5967368-9c1c-5296-b137-b9913b855878" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424255 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424251 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424255 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110816" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424255 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424255 #edb/ref 1071 "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $a$ | $2a$ | $\\frac{3a}{2}$ | $3a$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above. Find the value of $a.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424255 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0c6d1e5f-c8c7-58eb-9372-45bad8d48254" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424255 #edb/ref 1074 "The support of $X$ is ${S}_{X}=\\{2\\},$ the support of $Y$ is ${S}_{Y}=\\{0,1,2,3\\},$ and therefore the joint support $S$ is\n\n$$\nS={S}_{X}\\times {S}_{Y}=\\{(2,0),(2,1),(2,2),(2,3)\\}.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a joint probability distribution $f(x,y),$ we must have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2,0)+f(2,1)+f(2,2)+f(2,3) & =1 \\\\ a+2a+\\frac{3a}{2}+3a & =1 \\\\ \\frac{15a}{2} & =1 \\\\ a & =\\frac{2}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424256 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424254 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424256 #edb/ref 1069 "q-111038" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424256 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424256 #edb/ref 1071 "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |\n\nCompute $P(X>0\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,Y<2)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424256 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "663c80f0-fe5e-502f-84c3-e0164d0d760f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424256 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>0\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,Y<2) & =P((X,Y)\\in \\{(1,0),(1,1),(2,0),(2,1)\\}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(1,0))+P((X,Y)=(1,1)) \\\\  & \\,+P((X,Y)=(2,0))+P((X,Y)=(2,1)) \\\\  & =f(1,0)+f(1,1)+f(2,0)+f(2,1) \\\\  & =0.1+0.05+0.15+0.05 \\\\  & =0.35.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424257 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424252 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424257 #edb/ref 1069 "q-111035" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424257 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424257 #edb/ref 1071 "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n\nCompute $P(0<Y<2)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424257 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "77b7b7f9-a7fd-5ac7-a5d0-130bc06dad6a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424257 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0<Y<2) & =P(Y=1) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)\\in \\{(0,1),(1,1)\\}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(0,1))+P((X,Y)=(1,1)) \\\\  & =f(0,1)+f(1,1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424258 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424253 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424258 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110814" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424258 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424258 #edb/ref 1071 "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{a}{3}$ | $a$ | $3a$ |\n| $X=1$ | $4a$ | $\\frac{2a}{3}$ | $\\frac{a}{2}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $a$ | $\\frac{3a}{2}$ | $5a$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above. Find the value of $a.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424258 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f92de356-71ac-5b5e-9291-a3c3ef80d00b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424258 #edb/ref 1074 "The support of $X$ is ${S}_{X}=\\{0,1,2\\},$ the support of $Y$ is ${S}_{Y}=\\{0,1,2\\},$ and therefore the joint support $S$ is\n\n$$\nS={S}_{X}\\times {S}_{Y}=\\{(0,0),(0,1),(0,2),(1,0),(1,1),(1,2),(2,0),(2,1),(2,2)\\}.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a joint probability distribution $f(x,y),$ we must have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,0)+f(0,1)+f(0,2)+f(1,0)+f(1,1)+f(1,2)+f(2,0)+f(2,1)+f(2,2) & =1 \\\\ \\frac{a}{3}+a+3a+4a+\\frac{2a}{3}+\\frac{a}{2}+a+\\frac{3a}{2}+5a & =1 \\\\ 17a & =1 \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{17}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
